Built in San Francisco as a label, event series, and radio station, program audio has become a prominent ecosystem within the city's electronic music landscape. Founded by Bay Area natives Arthur Javier and Erika Martinez, its work has been featured in Mixmag, Resident Advisor, the SF Chronicle, KQED, and SFGate.

The collective: erika, sfcowboy, moth, and lexicon take that sound from warehouses to renegade campouts across the US and beyond, bringing eclectic sound and energy that shaped program audio at home.

