Night & Day returns with a lineup spanning several corners of the techno spectrum. Berlin’s Janina has been behind the decks at Club der Visionäre since she was 18, establishing herself as one of the venue’s defining residents with a deep-rooted approach to house and techno. Copenhagen’s Peachlyfe brings a psychedelic soundscape to the dancefloor, moving between trance, experimental techno, and high-energy rhythmic explorations. London’s Yazzus draws on ’90s techno, electro, and the history of UK rave culture, known for fast-paced, genre-fluid sets that balance intensity with experimentation. Annie Lew and Signal resident 98dots round out the main room, bringing their own perspectives on underground dance music to the extended session. In AUX, Kokölò hosts a label showcase with Adriana Ruas and Alfonsvs.

